 p=P.read_text();p=re.sub(r'object%20accounting-[0-9.]+%25','object%20accounting-90.90%25',p,count=1);p=re.sub(r'\*\*Verified translated instruction bytes:\*\* \*\*[0-9,]+\*\*','**Verified translated instruction bytes:** **213,623**',p,count=1);p=re.sub(r'\*\*Proven non-code/data bytes:\*\* \*\*[0-9,]+\*\*','**Proven non-code/data bytes:** **4,269**',p,count=1);p=re.sub(r'\*\*Reconciled object bytes:\*\* \*\*[0-9,]+ / 239,698 = [0-9.]+% \([0-9.]+%\)\*\*','**Reconciled object bytes:** **217,892 / 239,698 = 90.9027% (90.90%)**',p,count=1);p=re.sub(r'\*\*Unresolved object bytes:\*\* \*\*[0-9,]+\*\*','**Unresolved object bytes:** **21,806**',p,count=1);P.write_text(norm(p.rstrip()+'''\n## Batch 92 — weighted-word lookup\n\nAdded **63 translated instruction bytes** and **1 alignment byte**, bringing accounting to **213,623 translated + 4,269 non-code = 217,892 / 239,698 = 90.9027% (90.90%)**. `337C8` sign-extends the starting byte at `25621`, walks a word-weight array at `table+102h+slot`, accumulates through the 16-bit `CX` subregister, and compares the zero-extended wrapped sum against the signed target. The post-loop second `SUB EBX,2` and unsigned-borrow clamp are preserved, including the exhaustion path that can retain a negative displacement. Next frontier: **`33808`**.\n'''))
 a=A.read_text();A.write_text(norm(a.rstrip()+'''\n## CODE.2 Batch 92 checkpoint\n\nBatch 92 reconciles `337C8..33807`: **63 translated + 1 alignment byte**. Coverage is **217,892 / 239,698 = 90.9027% (90.90%)**, with **21,806 unresolved bytes**. Preserve signed-byte slot initialization, 16-bit wrapping `CX` accumulation, signed `CMP ECX,EDX / JGE`, the signed loop test after the first `SUB EBX,2`, and the separate unsigned-borrow test after the second subtraction. Next frontier is `33808`.\n'''))
